## 11. Lessons Learned

### 11.1 What Went Well

1. **Comprehensive test coverage** - All 77 test cases executed (100%)
2. **Evidence collection** - Every test documented with screenshots/videos
3. **Intentional defect detection** - 2/10 found despite 60% blocked
4. **Accessibility testing** - Strong coverage with axe DevTools and screen readers
5. **Cross-browser testing** - Tested on 3 major browsers
6. **Team collaboration** - Effective role distribution and communication

### 11.2 Challenges Faced

1. **Missing features** - 34% of tests blocked by unimplemented features
2. **Admin system broken** - Severe impact on testing workflow
3. **No Safari access** - Could not test Safari compatibility
4. **Localhost limitations** - PageSpeed Insights unavailable
5. **Payment issues** - Difficulty verifying Paystack integration
6. **Time constraints** - 14 days insufficient for comprehensive testing with blockers

### 11.3 Key Insights

1. **Feature completeness matters** - Missing features blocked 26 test cases (34%)
2. **Early admin testing** - Admin system defects discovered late
3. **Cross-browser issues widespread** - 88% compatibility failure rate
4. **Intentional defects challenging** - Only 20% found, 60% blocked by missing features
5. **Performance optimization needed** - LCP and TTI exceed targets

